From 666a469576eaa077ec893dba29c3a0f463d82722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:23:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ui): 3D tool preview flutes for each kind, a finer
 mesh, part inks

The tool library's 3D preview cuts flutes into every milling cutter
with a cutting length, the twist drill and the tap (a drill or tap
without a count draws its kind's count). The preview revolve takes 96
facets around instead of 32. The cutting part, the shank and the
holder each take a new theme ink (tool_model_flute, tool_model_shank,
tool_model_holder), shaded by the light. The Properties side preview
draws a thread mill's teeth too. Display only: no toolpath, collision,
simulation or posted output changes.

Fixes #4452

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
